---
import DocsLayout from '../../layouts/DocsLayout.astro';
import CodeBlock from '../../components/CodeBlock.astro';

const headings = [
  { id: 'gui', text: 'GUI', level: 2 },
  { id: 'export', text: 'Export', level: 2 },
  { id: 'flags', text: 'Flags', level: 2 },
];
---

<DocsLayout title="CLI" headings={headings}>
  <p>The <code>markrust</code> binary provides both the desktop application and command-line utilities.</p>

  <h2 id="gui">GUI</h2>
  <CodeBlock code="markrust" terminal />
  <p>Launches the MarkRust editor. This is the default when no subcommand is given.</p>

  <h2 id="export">Export</h2>
  <CodeBlock code={`markrust export README.md\nmarkrust export README.md -o dist/README.html\nmarkrust export trusted.md --unsafe-html`} terminal />
  <p>Converts a Markdown file to HTML using comrak with GFM extensions. Output defaults to a <code>.html</code> file beside the source.</p>
  <p>Exports are safe by default: raw HTML and dangerous URL schemes are omitted. Use <code>--unsafe-html</code> only for Markdown you trust and intentionally want to preserve raw HTML and dangerous URLs; GFM tag filtering still applies.</p>

  <h2 id="flags">Flags</h2>
  <CodeBlock code={`markrust --version\nmarkrust --help\nmarkrust --gui    # explicit GUI launch\nmarkrust export --unsafe-html trusted.md`} terminal />
</DocsLayout>
